-- title:
--   Degree-zero divisors as residue divisors of differentials
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero and let $F$ be a field which is a $K$-algebra, subject to the hypothesis `hfg` that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ and $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume `IsCurveOver K F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has a finitely supported divisor of degree zero recording its orders $v.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ at all places, every residue field $v.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is a finite $K$-module, and $\Omega[F\!\mid\!K]$ is free of rank one over $F$; assume also `HasCanonicalDivisor`, i.e. every nonzero $\omega \in \Omega[F\!\mid\!K]$ has a finitely supported divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\,\omega$. Here a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$, which is a principal ideal ring; $v.\mathrm{differentialCoeff}\,\omega$ is the chosen $h \in F$ with $\omega = h \cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$ (where $v.\mathrm{dCoord} = d(v.\mathrm{uniformizer})$), or $0$ if none exists, and $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\,\omega$ is its order at $v$. Let $D$ be a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on places with $\sum_v D(v)\deg v = 0$. Then there is $\eta \in \Omega[F\!\mid\!K]$ with $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\,\eta \ge -1$ for all places $v$, and such that for every $v$ the evaluation $\mathrm{evalAt}\ v$ of $v.\mathrm{dCoordFn} \cdot v.\mathrm{differentialCoeff}\,\eta$ — the $K$-value of the residue class of the element when it lies in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise — equals the image of the integer $D(v)$ in $K$. The element $v.\mathrm{dCoordFn}$ is the one chosen from the existence statement `exists_ord_eq_one_and_dCoord_eq` attached to $v$.
--
--   This is the classical existence of differentials of the third kind with prescribed residues: a degree-zero divisor on a curve over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero is the residue divisor of a differential with at worst simple poles, the residue at $v$ being expressed intrinsically as the value at $v$ of the product of the local parameter with the coefficient of $\eta$. It is used in the Abel–Jacobi step [`AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.isPrincipal_of_abelJacobiDiv_mem_pathPeriodLattice`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.isPrincipal_of_abelJacobiDiv_mem_pathPeriodLattice), and rests on Riemann–Roch for $F/K$ together with the residue theorem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_ordDifferential_ge_neg_one_and_evalAt_eq_of_degree_eq_zero.lean

